# Docker build context excludes (Increment 14b). The build context is the repo ROOT for both the
# apps/api and apps/web images; each Dockerfile COPYies only the workspaces it needs. These excludes
# keep the context small and ensure NO secrets or host-built artifacts ever enter an image.
# (Railway's upload already honours .gitignore; this is the docker-build layer.)

# Dependencies (re-installed in-image)
**/node_modules

# Build outputs (re-built in-image)
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/.expo
**/.expo-shared
**/.turbo
**/out
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets / env — NEVER copy these into an image
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
**/google-service-account*.json
**/serviceAccountKey*.json

# VCS / CI / editor / OS
.git
.github
.vscode
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Tests / coverage / logs
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/*.log

# Native build artifacts
**/ios/Pods
**/android/.gradle
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
